als without writing a raw timer callback yourself?", "token_count": 21, "processing_duration_ms": 225}, "context": {"chunks": [{"chunk_id": "adc2e3af-3e16-40a0-a2fa-ccd4e3c069a8", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 5, "section": "Schedulers", "content": "that provides a scheduler with an expression for relative time. Routing Notifications to Combine Subscribers\nDeliver notifications to subscribers by using notification centers\u02bc publishers. Replacing Foundation Timers with Timer Publishers\nPublish elements periodically by using a timer. Performing Key-Value Observing with Combine\nExpose KVO changes with a Combine publisher. Using Combine for Your App\u02bcs Asynchronous Code\nApply common patterns to migrate your closure-based, event-handling code.", "token_count": 86, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}, {"chunk_id": "f8aa5f53-44af-4282-9763-ee84f213ae70", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "content": "the values received from upstream publishers\nand republish them. At the end of a chain of publishers, a Subscriber acts on elements as it receives them. Publishers only emit values when explicitly requested to do so by subscribers. This puts\nyour subscriber code in control of how fast it receives events from the publishers it\u02bcs\nconnected to. Several Foundation types expose their functionality through publishers, including Timer,\nNotificationCenter, and URLSession.", "token_count": 93, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}, {"chunk_id": "ad2ad6a2-e768-43f9-a28f-86929b6041d0", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 4, "section": "Subscribers", "content": "le value and publishes a new element whenever the value\nchanges. class PassthroughSubject\nA subject that broadcasts elements to downstream subscribers. protocol Scheduler\nA protocol that defines when and how to execute a closure. struct ImmediateScheduler\nA scheduler for performing synchronous actions. Subjects\nSchedulers\nprotocol SchedulerTimeIntervalConvertible\nA protocol that provides a scheduler with an expression for relative time.", "token_count": 77, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}, {"chunk_id": "0725be3e-f12c-40f7-b124-101a41eaf47f", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "content": "The Combine framework provides a declarative Swift API for processing values over time. These values can represent many kinds of asynchronous events. Combine declares\npublishers to expose values that can change over time, and subscribers to receive those\nvalues from the publishers. The Publisher protocol declares a type that can deliver a sequence of values over\ntime. Publishers have operators to act on the values received from upstream publishers\nand republish them.", "token_count": 96, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}, {"chunk_id": "07bd3afc-3c2f-4085-8464-3cb87fde2a0f", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 5, "section": "Using Combine for Your App\u02bcs Asynchronous Code", "content": "mon patterns to migrate your closure-based, event-handling code. protocol ObservableObject\nA type of object with a publisher that emits before the object has changed. class ObservableObjectPublisher\nA publisher that publishes changes from observable objects. struct AsyncPublisher\nA publisher that exposes its elements as an asynchronous sequence. struct AsyncThrowingPublisher\nA publisher that exposes its elements as a throwing asynchronous sequence.", "token_count": 78, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}], "total_tokens": 430, "chunk_count": 5, "document_count": 1}, "prompt": {"system": "You are a RAG assi