ers. protocol Scheduler\nA protocol that defines when and how to execute a closure. struct ImmediateScheduler\nA scheduler for performing synchronous actions. Subjects\nSchedulers\nprotocol SchedulerTimeIntervalConvertible\nA protocol that provides a scheduler with an expression for relative time.\n\n[Source 4] Document: Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf, Page: 1, Chunk: 0725be3e-f12c-40f7-b124-101a41eaf47f\nThe Combine framework provides a declarative Swift API for processing values over time. These values can represent many kinds of asynchronous events. Combine declares\npublishers to expose values that can change over time, and subscribers to receive those\nvalues from the publishers. The Publisher protocol declares a type that can deliver a sequence of values over\ntime. Publishers have operators to act on the values received from upstream publishers\nand republish them.\n\n[Source 5] Document: Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf, Page: 5, Chunk: 07bd3afc-3c2f-4085-8464-3cb87fde2a0f, Section: Using Combine for Your App\u02bcs Asynchronous Code\nmon patterns to migrate your closure-based, event-handling code. protocol ObservableObject\nA type of object with a publisher that emits before the object has changed. class ObservableObjectPublisher\nA publisher that publishes changes from observable objects. struct AsyncPublisher\nA publisher that exposes its elements as an asynchronous sequence. struct AsyncThrowingPublisher\nA publisher that exposes its elements as a throwing asynchronous sequence.\n</context>", "user": "How can values be emitted at regular time intervals without writing a raw timer callback yourself?", "system_tokens": 105, "context_tokens": 530, "user_tokens": 21, "total_tokens": 656}, "llm": {"provider": "groq", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "latency_ms": 7185, "input_tokens": null, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": null, "answer": "You can use Combine\u2019s built\u2011in **Timer publisher**.\u202fIt creates a publisher that emits elements on a regular schedule, so you get periodic values without writing a manual timer callback yourself\u202f[Source\u202f1]\u202fand\u202f[Source\u202f2].", "status": "completed"}, "sources": [{"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 5, "section": "Schedulers", "chunk_id": "adc2e3af-3e16-40a0-a2fa-ccd4e3c069a8", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "chunk_id": "f8aa5f53-44af-4282-9763-ee84f213ae70", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 4, "section": "Subscribers", "chunk_id": "ad2ad6a2-e768-43f9-a28f-86929b6041d0", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "chunk_id": "0725be3e-f12c-40f7-b124-101a41eaf47f", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 5, "section": "Using Combine for Your App\u02bcs Asynchronous Code", "chunk_id": "07bd3afc-3c2f-4085-8464-3cb87fde2a0f", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}], "total_latency_ms": 7410, "status": "completed", "error": null, "vector_search": {"latency_ms": 0, "chunk_count": 5, "results": [{"chunk_id": "adc2e3af-3e16-40a0-a2fa-ccd4e3c069a8", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 5, "score": 0.4321886891848192, "rank": 1}, {"chunk_id": "f8aa5f53-44af-4282-9763-ee84f213ae70", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "score": 0.41438424456664386, "rank": 2}, {"chunk_id": "ad2ad6a2-e768-43f9-a28f-86