"event": "mmr.selection.updated", "data": {"chunk_id": "c6628529-8448-47ae-a23f-cb59c0edee68", "rank": 5, "mmr_score": 0.04527474026881183, "relevance_score": 0.04527474026881183, "selected": true}, "timestamp": "2026-09-03T16:51:49.536064+00:00"}, {"stage": "mmr", "event": "mmr.completed", "data": {"selected_count": 5, "rejected_count": 0}, "timestamp": "2026-09-03T16:51:49.536066+00:00"}, {"stage": "context", "event": "context.built", "data": {"chunk_count": 5, "document_count": 2, "total_tokens": 419}, "timestamp": "2026-09-03T16:51:49.536076+00:00"}, {"stage": "prompt", "event": "prompt.built", "data": {"system_tokens": 105, "context_tokens": 510, "user_tokens": 26, "total_tokens": 641}, "timestamp": "2026-09-03T16:51:49.536159+00:00"}, {"stage": "llm", "event": "llm.started", "data": {"model": "gemini-2.0-flash", "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": 1024}, "timestamp": "2026-09-03T16:51:49.536243+00:00"}, {"stage": "llm", "event": "trace.failed", "data": {"error": "gemini API error (404): [{\n  \"error\": {\n    \"code\": 404,\n    \"message\": \"This model models/gemini-2.0-flash is no longer available. Please update your code to use models/gemini-3.6-flash for the latest features and improvements. We recommend you to use the Interactions API.\",\n    \"status\": \"NOT_FOUND\"\n  }\n}\n]"}, "timestamp": "2026-09-03T16:51:49.718150+00:00"}, {"stage": "llm", "event": "llm.completed", "data": {"model": "gemini-2.0-flash", "latency_ms": 181, "status": "failed", "error": "gemini API error (404): [{\n  \"error\": {\n    \"code\": 404,\n    \"message\": \"This model models/gemini-2.0-flash is no longer available. Please update your code to use models/gemini-3.6-flash for the latest features and improvements. We recommend you to use the Interactions API.\",\n    \"status\": \"NOT_FOUND\"\n  }\n}\n]"}, "timestamp": "2026-09-03T16:51:49.718167+00:00"}], "query_processing": {"original_query": "What protocol would you conform to if you needed custom logic for turning Swift values into a serialized data format?", "token_count": 26, "processing_duration_ms": 122}, "context": {"chunks": [{"chunk_id": "0725be3e-f12c-40f7-b124-101a41eaf47f", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "content": "The Combine framework provides a declarative Swift API for processing values over time. These values can represent many kinds of asynchronous events. Combine declares\npublishers to expose values that can change over time, and subscribers to receive those\nvalues from the publishers. The Publisher protocol declares a type that can deliver a sequence of values over\ntime. Publishers have operators to act on the values received from upstream publishers\nand republish them.", "token_count": 96, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}, {"chunk_id": "2e1daa1b-ece7-4af3-99a3-04b479fc879b", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 2, "section": "Combine", "content": "S 6.0+\nDocumentation Language:Swift\nuse them to update your app. By adopting Combine, you\u02bcll make your code easier to read and maintain, by centralizing\nyour event-processing code and eliminating troublesome techniques like nested closures\nand convention-based callbacks. Receiving and Handling Events with Combine\nCustomize and receive events from asynchronous sources. protocol Publisher\nDeclares that a type can transmit a sequence of values over time.", "token_count": 85, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}, {"chunk_id": "b8facd33-692a-4ffd-9f3e-168f3f78d04f", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "content": "ext field\u02bcs publisher, and use the text to\nperform URL requests. You can then use another publisher to process the responses and\nOverview\nFramework\nCombine\nCustomize handling of asynchronous events by combining event-\nprocessing operators. iOS 13.0+ iPadOS 13.0+ Mac Catalyst 13.0+macOS 10.15+ tvOS 13.0+ visionOS 1.0+\nwatchOS 6.0+\nDocumentation Language:Swift\nuse them to update your app.", "token_count": 76, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}, {"chunk_id": "e1f33e2b-8b41-4e9a-ac31-9f392f45f238", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 6, "section": "Using Combine for Your App\u02bcs Asynchronous Code", "content": "r that exposes its elements as a throwing asynchronous sequence. Combine Migration\nObservable Objects\nAsynchronous Publishers\nEncoders and Decoders\nprotocol TopLevelEncoder\nA type that defines methods for encoding. protocol TopLevelDecoder\nA type that defines methods for decoding. protocol CustomCombineIdentifierConvertible\nA protocol for uniquely identifying publisher streams. struct CombineIdentifier\nA unique identifier for identifying publisher streams. Debugging Identifiers", "token_count": 76, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}, {"chunk_id": "c6628529-8448-47ae-a23f-cb59c0edee68", "document_id": "359ced78-31ba-4192-93dc-c1b9919a4f8a", "document_name": "current-version.md", "page": 1, "section": null, "content": "f `204 No Content`; the deletion is processed in the background. > **Migrating from 2022-11-28:** treat `202` as success, not just `204` \u2014 the installation may not be fully removed the instant the response is received. ## GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/code-scanning/default-setup\n\nThe `languages` array no longer contains `javascript` and `typescript` as separate values \u2014 they are combined into a single **`javascript-typescript`** value, since CodeQL analyzes them together.", "token_count": 86, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}], "total_tokens": 419, "chunk_count": 5, "document_count": 2}, "prompt": {"system": "You are a RAG assistant. Answer only using the text inside <context> tags below.\n\nRules:\n- If the answer is not i