o Combine Subscribers\nDeliver notifications to subscribers by using notification centers\u02bc publishers. Replacing Foundation Timers with Timer Publishers\nPublish elements periodically by using a timer. Performing Key-Value Observing with Combine\nExpose KVO changes with a Combine publisher. Using Combine for Your App\u02bcs Asynchronous Code\nApply common patterns to migrate your closure-based, event-handling code.\n\n[Source 3] Document: Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf, Page: 1, Chunk: f8aa5f53-44af-4282-9763-ee84f213ae70\nthe values received from upstream publishers\nand republish them. At the end of a chain of publishers, a Subscriber acts on elements as it receives them. Publishers only emit values when explicitly requested to do so by subscribers. This puts\nyour subscriber code in control of how fast it receives events from the publishers it\u02bcs\nconnected to. Several Foundation types expose their functionality through publishers, including Timer,\nNotificationCenter, and URLSession.\n\n[Source 4] Document: Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf, Page: 1, Chunk: eb603e2c-4ed9-42e6-b039-92056b6c568e\npublishers, including Timer,\nNotificationCenter, and URLSession. Combine also provides a built-in publisher for\nany property that\u02bcs compliant with Key-Value Observing. You can combine the output of multiple publishers and coordinate their interaction. For\nexample, you can subscribe to updates from a text field\u02bcs publisher, and use the text to\nperform URL requests.\n\n[Source 5] Document: current-version.md, Page: 1, Chunk: c6628529-8448-47ae-a23f-cb59c0edee68\nf `204 No Content`; the deletion is processed in the background. > **Migrating from 2022-11-28:** treat `202` as success, not just `204` \u2014 the installation may not be fully removed the instant the response is received. ## GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/code-scanning/default-setup\n\nThe `languages` array no longer contains `javascript` and `typescript` as separate values \u2014 they are combined into a single **`javascript-typescript`** value, since CodeQL analyzes them together.\n</context>", "user": "What are the benefits of adopting Combine in your code?", "system_tokens": 105, "context_tokens": 504, "user_tokens": 13, "total_tokens": 622}, "llm": {"provider": "groq", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "latency_ms": 901, "input_tokens": null, "output_tokens": 38, "total_tokens": null, "answer": "Adopting Combine makes your code easier to read and maintain by centralizing event\u2011processing logic and removing troublesome patterns such as nested closures and convention\u2011based callbacks\u3010Source 1\u3011.", "status": "completed"}, "sources": [{"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 2, "section": "Combine", "chunk_id": "2e1daa1b-ece7-4af3-99a3-04b479fc879b", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 5, "section": "Schedulers", "chunk_id": "adc2e3af-3e16-40a0-a2fa-ccd4e3c069a8", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "chunk_id": "f8aa5f53-44af-4282-9763-ee84f213ae70", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "chunk_id": "eb603e2c-4ed9-42e6-b039-92056b6c568e", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "359ced78-31ba-4192-93dc-c1b9919a4f8a", "document_name": "current-version.md", "page": 1, "section": null, "chunk_id": "c6628529-8448-47ae-a23f-cb59c0edee68", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}], "total_latency_ms": 903, "status": "completed", "error": null, "vector_search": null, "bm25": {"lat