s a built-in publisher for\nany property that\u02bcs compliant with Key-Value Observing. You can combine the output of multiple publishers and coordinate their interaction. For\nexample, you can subscribe to updates from a text field\u02bcs publisher, and use the text to\nperform URL requests.\n\n[Source 4] Document: Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf, Page: 4, Chunk: a68a13c0-41b2-4f66-820b-d0638841b05f, Section: Subscribers\nas subscribers. struct AnySubscriber\nA type-erasing subscriber. protocol Subscription\nA protocol representing the connection of a subscriber to a publisher. enum Subscriptions\nA namespace for symbols related to subscriptions. protocol Subject\nA publisher that exposes a method for outside callers to publish elements. class CurrentValueSubject\nA subject that wraps a single value and publishes a new element whenever the value\nchanges.\n\n[Source 5] Document: Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf, Page: 2, Chunk: 2e1daa1b-ece7-4af3-99a3-04b479fc879b, Section: Combine\nS 6.0+\nDocumentation Language:Swift\nuse them to update your app. By adopting Combine, you\u02bcll make your code easier to read and maintain, by centralizing\nyour event-processing code and eliminating troublesome techniques like nested closures\nand convention-based callbacks. Receiving and Handling Events with Combine\nCustomize and receive events from asynchronous sources. protocol Publisher\nDeclares that a type can transmit a sequence of values over time.\n</context>", "user": "How would system notifications be delivered to subscribers instead of using NotificationCenter's traditional observer API directly?", "system_tokens": 105, "context_tokens": 506, "user_tokens": 21, "total_tokens": 632}, "llm": {"provider": "groq", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "latency_ms": 7731, "input_tokens": null, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": null, "answer": "System notifications can be delivered to Combine subscribers by using NotificationCenter\u2019s built\u2011in publishers\u2014creating a publisher from the notification you\u2019re interested in and subscribing to it\u2014rather than adding observers with the traditional NotificationCenter API.\u202f[Source\u202f1]", "status": "completed"}, "sources": [{"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 5, "section": "Schedulers", "chunk_id": "adc2e3af-3e16-40a0-a2fa-ccd4e3c069a8", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "chunk_id": "f8aa5f53-44af-4282-9763-ee84f213ae70", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "chunk_id": "eb603e2c-4ed9-42e6-b039-92056b6c568e", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 4, "section": "Subscribers", "chunk_id": "a68a13c0-41b2-4f66-820b-d0638841b05f", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 2, "section": "Combine", "chunk_id": "2e1daa1b-ece7-4af3-99a3-04b479fc879b", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}], "total_latency_ms": 7964, "status": "completed", "error": null, "vector_search": {"latency_ms": 0, "chunk_count": 5, "results": [{"chunk_id": "adc2e3af-3e16-40a0-a2fa-ccd4e3c069a8", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 5, "score": 0.552115175620806, "rank": 1}, {"chunk_id": "f8aa5f53-44af-4282-9763-ee84f213ae70", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "score": 0.4269866961095365, "rank": 2}, {"chunk_id": "eb603e2c-4ed9-42e6-b039-92056b6c5