 {"model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "latency_ms": 605, "status": "completed"}, "timestamp": "2026-09-03T08:04:49.386640+00:00"}], "query_processing": {"original_query": "What is AnyPublisher in Combine?", "token_count": 6, "processing_duration_ms": 1}, "context": {"chunks": [{"chunk_id": "eb603e2c-4ed9-42e6-b039-92056b6c568e", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "content": "publishers, including Timer,\nNotificationCenter, and URLSession. Combine also provides a built-in publisher for\nany property that\u02bcs compliant with Key-Value Observing. You can combine the output of multiple publishers and coordinate their interaction. For\nexample, you can subscribe to updates from a text field\u02bcs publisher, and use the text to\nperform URL requests.", "token_count": 69, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}, {"chunk_id": "b466ce24-567f-442d-8453-9eef4bb4d722", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 2, "section": "Receiving and Handling Events with Combine", "content": "eclares that a type can transmit a sequence of values over time. enum Publishers\nA namespace for types that serve as publishers. struct AnyPublisher\nA publisher that performs type erasure by wrapping another publisher. struct Published\nA type that publishes a property marked with an attribute. protocol Cancellable\nA protocol indicating that an activity or action supports cancellation. class AnyCancellable\nA type-erasing cancellable object that executes a provided closure when canceled.", "token_count": 94, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}, {"chunk_id": "f8aa5f53-44af-4282-9763-ee84f213ae70", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "content": "the values received from upstream publishers\nand republish them. At the end of a chain of publishers, a Subscriber acts on elements as it receives them. Publishers only emit values when explicitly requested to do so by subscribers. This puts\nyour subscriber code in control of how fast it receives events from the publishers it\u02bcs\nconnected to. Several Foundation types expose their functionality through publishers, including Timer,\nNotificationCenter, and URLSession.", "token_count": 93, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}, {"chunk_id": "adc2e3af-3e16-40a0-a2fa-ccd4e3c069a8", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 5, "section": "Schedulers", "content": "that provides a scheduler with an expression for relative time. Routing Notifications to Combine Subscribers\nDeliver notifications to subscribers by using notification centers\u02bc publishers. Replacing Foundation Timers with Timer Publishers\nPublish elements periodically by using a timer. Performing Key-Value Observing with Combine\nExpose KVO changes with a Combine publisher. Using Combine for Your App\u02bcs Asynchronous Code\nApply common patterns to migrate your closure-based, event-handling code.", "token_count": 86, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}, {"chunk_id": "2e1daa1b-ece7-4af3-99a3-04b479fc879b", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 2, "section": "Combine", "content": "S 6.0+\nDocumentation Language:Swift\nuse them to update your app. By adopting Combine, you\u02bcll make your code easier to read and maintain, by centralizing\nyour event-processing code and eliminating troublesome techniques like nested closures\nand convention-based callbacks. Receiving and Handling Events with Combine\nCustomize and receive events from asynchronous sources. protocol Publisher\nDeclares that a type can transmit a sequence of values over time.", "token_count": 85, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}], "tot