, {"stage": "context", "event": "context.built", "data": {"chunk_count": 5, "document_count": 1, "total_tokens": 425}, "timestamp": "2026-09-03T07:39:06.714081+00:00"}, {"stage": "prompt", "event": "prompt.built", "data": {"system_tokens": 105, "context_tokens": 520, "user_tokens": 10, "total_tokens": 635}, "timestamp": "2026-09-03T07:39:06.714130+00:00"}, {"stage": "llm", "event": "llm.started", "data": {"model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": 1024}, "timestamp": "2026-09-03T07:39:06.714166+00:00"}, {"stage": "llm", "event": "llm.completed", "data": {"model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "latency_ms": 568, "status": "completed"}, "timestamp": "2026-09-03T07:39:07.282248+00:00"}], "query_processing": {"original_query": "What kind of rendering does Core Graphics provide?", "token_count": 10, "processing_duration_ms": 0}, "context": {"chunks": [{"chunk_id": "f8aa5f53-44af-4282-9763-ee84f213ae70", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "content": "the values received from upstream publishers\nand republish them. At the end of a chain of publishers, a Subscriber acts on elements as it receives them. Publishers only emit values when explicitly requested to do so by subscribers. This puts\nyour subscriber code in control of how fast it receives events from the publishers it\u02bcs\nconnected to. Several Foundation types expose their functionality through publishers, including Timer,\nNotificationCenter, and URLSession.", "token_count": 93, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}, {"chunk_id": "d9f2ebad-d428-47d1-8da0-12cde93f279a", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 3, "section": "Publishers", "content": "never publishes any values, and optionally finishes immediately. struct Fail\nA publisher that immediately terminates with the specified error. struct Record\nA publisher that allows for recording a series of inputs and a completion, for later\nplayback to each subscriber. Controlling Publishing with Connectable Publishers\nCoordinate when publishers start sending elements to subscribers. protocol ConnectablePublisher\nA publisher that provides an explicit means of connecting and canceling publication.", "token_count": 89, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}, {"chunk_id": "0725be3e-f12c-40f7-b124-101a41eaf47f", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "content": "The Combine framework provides a declarative Swift API for processing values over time. These values can represent many kinds of asynchronous events. Combine declares\npublishers to expose values that can change over time, and subscribers to receive those\nvalues from the publishers. The Publisher protocol declares a type that can deliver a sequence of values over\ntime. Publishers have operators to act on the values received from upstream publishers\nand republish them.", "token_count": 96, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}, {"chunk_id": "eb603e2c-4ed9-42e6-b039-92056b6c568e", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "content": "publishers, including Timer,\nNotificationCenter, and URLSession. Combine also provides a built-in publisher for\nany property that\u02bcs compliant with Key-Value Observing. You can combine the output of multiple publishers and coordinate their interaction. For\nexample, you can subscribe to updates from a text field\u02bcs publisher, and use the text to\nperform URL requests.", "token_count": 69, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}, {"chunk_id": "71a5e0c9-96df-4809-9d7c-e4e39eebcb38", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 3, "section": "Controlling