cified error. struct Record\nA publisher that allows for recording a series of inputs and a completion, for later\nplayback to each subscriber. Controlling Publishing with Connectable Publishers\nCoordinate when publishers start sending elements to subscribers. protocol ConnectablePublisher\nA publisher that provides an explicit means of connecting and canceling publication.\n\n[Source 3] Document: Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf, Page: 1, Chunk: 0725be3e-f12c-40f7-b124-101a41eaf47f\nThe Combine framework provides a declarative Swift API for processing values over time. These values can represent many kinds of asynchronous events. Combine declares\npublishers to expose values that can change over time, and subscribers to receive those\nvalues from the publishers. The Publisher protocol declares a type that can deliver a sequence of values over\ntime. Publishers have operators to act on the values received from upstream publishers\nand republish them.\n\n[Source 4] Document: Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf, Page: 1, Chunk: eb603e2c-4ed9-42e6-b039-92056b6c568e\npublishers, including Timer,\nNotificationCenter, and URLSession. Combine also provides a built-in publisher for\nany property that\u02bcs compliant with Key-Value Observing. You can combine the output of multiple publishers and coordinate their interaction. For\nexample, you can subscribe to updates from a text field\u02bcs publisher, and use the text to\nperform URL requests.\n\n[Source 5] Document: Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf, Page: 3, Chunk: 71a5e0c9-96df-4809-9d7c-e4e39eebcb38, Section: Controlling Publishing with Connectable Publishers\nvides an explicit means of connecting and canceling publication. Processing Published Elements with Subscribers\nApply back pressure\u00a0to precisely control when publishers produce elements. Convenience Publishers\nConnectable Publishers\nSubscribers\nprotocol Subscriber\nA protocol that declares a type that can receive input from a publisher. enum Subscribers\nA namespace for types that serve as subscribers. struct AnySubscriber\nA type-erasing subscriber.\n</context>", "user": "What kind of rendering does Core Graphics provide?", "system_tokens": 105, "context_tokens": 520, "user_tokens": 10, "total_tokens": 635}, "llm": {"provider": "groq", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "latency_ms": 568, "input_tokens": null, "output_tokens": 11, "total_tokens": null, "answer": "I could not find that information in the provided documents.", "status": "completed"}, "sources": [{"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "chunk_id": "f8aa5f53-44af-4282-9763-ee84f213ae70", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 3, "section": "Publishers", "chunk_id": "d9f2ebad-d428-47d1-8da0-12cde93f279a", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "chunk_id": "0725be3e-f12c-40f7-b124-101a41eaf47f", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "chunk_id": "eb603e2c-4ed9-42e6-b039-92056b6c568e", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 3, "section": "Controlling Publishing with Connectable Publishers", "chunk_id": "71a5e0c9-96df-4809-9d7c-e4e39eebcb38", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}], "total_latency_ms": 568, "status": "completed", "error": null, "vector_search": null, "bm25": {"latency_ms": 0, "chunk_count": 5, "query_terms": ["what", "kind", "of", "rendering