s a declarative Swift API for processing values over time. These values can represent many kinds of asynchronous events. Combine declares\npublishers to expose values that can change over time, and subscribers to receive those\nvalues from the publishers. The Publisher protocol declares a type that can deliver a sequence of values over\ntime.\n\n[Source 3] Document: Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf, Page: 3\nw fast it receives events from the publishers it\u02bcs\nconnected to. Several Foundation types expose their functionality through publishers, including Timer,\nNotificationCenter, and URLSession. Combine also provides a built-in publisher for\nany property that\u02bcs compliant with Key-Value Observing. You can combine the output of multiple publishers and coordinate their interaction. For\nexample, you can subscribe to updates from a text field\u02bcs publisher, and use the text to\nperform URL requests.\n</context>", "user": "What is Future and how does it differ from Just?", "system_tokens": 182, "context_tokens": 326, "user_tokens": 13, "total_tokens": 521}, "llm": {"provider": "groq", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "latency_ms": 2293, "input_tokens": null, "output_tokens": 11, "total_tokens": null, "answer": "I could not find that information in the provided documents.", "status": "completed"}, "sources": [{"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 2, "section": null, "chunk_id": "acd3d9b2-5d51-4a89-8311-6192ad9eee7c", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 1, "section": null, "chunk_id": "e72bd63e-d6e1-4caf-ad08-102bf2c8e8c8", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 3, "section": null, "chunk_id": "b