col indicating that an activity or action supports cancellation. class AnyCancellable\nA type-erasing cancellable object that executes a provided closure when canceled.", "token_count": 94, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}, {"chunk_id": "25e7b0a2-a776-4fd3-85d2-f39820d08e50", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 5, "section": null, "content": "as subscribers. struct AnySubscriber\nA type-erasing subscriber. protocol Subscription\nA protocol representing the connection of a subscriber to a publisher. enum Subscriptions\nA namespace for symbols related to subscriptions. protocol Subject\nA publisher that exposes a method for outside callers to publish elements. class CurrentValueSubject\nA subject that wraps a single value and publishes a new element whenever the value\nchanges.", "token_count": 81, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}, {"chunk_id": "66facfd0-ab11-4fc2-b529-567233ee3a68", "document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 4, "section": null, "content": "ext field\u02bcs publisher, and use the text to\nperform URL requests. You can then use another publisher to process the responses and\nOverview\nFramework\nCombine\nCustomize handling of asynchronous events by combining event-\nprocessing operators. iOS 13.0+ iPadOS 13.0+ Mac Catalyst 13.0+macOS 10.15+ tvOS 13.0+ visionOS 1.0+\nwatchOS 6.0+\nDocumentation Language:Swift\n26/08/26, 4:58\u202fPMCombine | Apple Developer Documentation\nPage 2 of 6https://developer.apple.com/documentation/combine\nuse them to update your app.", "token_count": 90, "score": 0.0, "method": "final"}], "total_tokens": 265, "chunk_count": 3, "document_count": 1}, "prompt": {"system": "STRICT CONTEXT-ONLY RULES:\n- Use only the text between <context> and </context>.\n- Never answer from general knowledge or assumptions.\n- If the context does not directly support the an