lishes a new element whenever the value\nchanges.\n\n[Source 2] Document: Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf, Page: 6\nle value and publishes a new element whenever the value\nchanges. class PassthroughSubject\nA subject that broadcasts elements to downstream subscribers. protocol Scheduler\nA protocol that defines when and how to execute a closure. struct ImmediateScheduler\nA scheduler for performing synchronous actions.\n\n[Source 3] Document: Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf, Page: 3\ninputs and a completion, for later\nplayback to each subscriber. Controlling Publishing with Connectable Publishers\nCoordinate when publishers start sending elements to subscribers. protocol ConnectablePublisher\nA publisher that provides an explicit means of connecting and canceling publication. Processing Published Elements with Subscribers\nApply back pressure\u00a0to precisely control when publishers produce elements.\n</context>", "user": "What is the purpose of the Subject protocol?", "system_tokens": 182, "context_tokens": 249, "user_tokens": 10, "total_tokens": 441}, "llm": {"provider": "groq", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "latency_ms": 4748, "input_tokens": null, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": null, "answer": "The\u202fSubject\u202fprotocol defines a publisher that lets external code publish elements into the stream\u2014it exposes a method so callers outside the publisher can emit values.\u202f[Source\u202f1]", "status": "completed"}, "sources": [{"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 5, "section": null, "chunk_id": "25e7b0a2-a776-4fd3-85d2-f39820d08e50", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "907f917b-3caa-4157-b94d-208635baaea9", "document_name": "Combine | Apple Developer Documentation.pdf", "page": 6, "section": null, "chunk_id": "03b815a5-f2e1-49ab-9787-ed569c2a0376", "retrieval_method": "final", "score": 0.0}, {"document_id": "